Dana H.: Kicking off POC with AtlasLedger. Use case: streaming txns -> FX enrichment via function/tool call -> append structured JSON per txn. Env: VPC + SAML SSO, 30d retention. Need Node sample, mapping of function outputs to SDK events, and two pricing options (hosted vs reserved) for ~1M tokens/mo, peak 400-600 qps. Timeline: 3 weeks.

Marco V.: Quick asks for kickoff email: confirm HSM requirement, IDP metadata, and whether outbound egress to the FX service is allowed from their VPC (and CIDRs).

Dana H.: They prefer HSM but will confirm. Egress allowed but via IP allowlist.

Isha P.: Node minimal example (streaming + function call):
```js
const { Redwood } = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const s = client.responses.stream({
  model: 'redwood-infer-pro-v1',
  input: 'Enrich txn with USD->EUR rate',
  stream: true,
  functions: [{
    name: 'fx_lookup',
    parameters: {
      type: 'object',
      properties: { pair: { type: 'string' }, rate: { type: 'number' }, ttl: { type: 'integer' } },
      required: ['pair','rate']
    }
  }],
  function_call: 'auto'
});
for await (const evt of s) {
  if (evt.type === 'function_call') {
    const tool = JSON.parse(evt.payload);
    // attach tool.rate and tool.ttl to the txn record
  }
  if (evt.type === 'delta') process.stdout.write(evt.chunk);
}
```
Notes: SDK emits discrete events: delta, function_call (payload is JSON string), end. Strongly recommend defining an explicit JSON schema in functions.parameters to avoid hallucinated/ambiguous fields. For Private deployments, consider the quantized variant (q4) to reduce cost.

Marco V.: Pricing rough: hosted on-demand ~ $0.02 / 1k tokens -> ~ $20/mo for 1M tokens. For sustained 400-600 qps peaks recommend Dedicated/reserved capacity: ballpark $7k - $11k / mo depending on model choice and p95 SLA. HSM-backed KMS on Private adds ~15-25% uplift. Expedited 2-week onboarding incurs a one-time fee.

Isha P.: Fallback & routing: set a routing policy that prefers Dedicated and falls back to hosted-compatible models. When falling back you retain function_call semantics but be aware of KMS key visibility and potential minor model output differences. Example policy (console YAML):
routes:
  - name: atlasledger-dedicated
    prefer: dedicated
    match: customer_id == "atlasledger"
  - name: atlasledger-hosted-fallback
    prefer: hosted
    fallback: true

Marco V.: Engineering gotchas to call out in the kickoff: 1) Outbound tool calls from Private need NAT/Egress or an in-VPC adaptor service; 2) Keep prompt + context <= ~1k tokens for predictable p95 latency, or enable KV/prefix caching to reduce token footprint; 3) Run a short eval to validate function output parity between reserved and hosted variants (tokenization and schema differences can matter).

PricingBot: I'll post a two-option quote (hosted vs 3mo reserved) plus expedited onboarding line in ~3 business hours.

SecBot: Uploaded security packet and SAML attribute map; IP allowlist template: https://redwood.internal/onboarding/ip-allowlist-template.md

